Wireshark build (Windows) complains about possible loss of precision:

warning C4267: '+=': conversion from 'size_t' to 'unsigned int', possible loss of data

outlen += (unsigned)clen;

static const char \*mka_ckn_info_uat_defaults\_\[\] = { NULL, NULL, "" };

uat_set_default_values(mka_ckn_info_uat, mka_ckn_info_uat_defaults\_);

prefs_register_uat_preference(mka_module, "ckn_info", "CAK/CKN Info", "A table to define CAKs and CKNs", mka_ckn_info_uat);

Not fond of making this part of the build configuration. This is not for development debug per se, but allows a 'behind the scene look' at what's going on. In case the worry is about the formatting overhead, the block can also be wrapped in the following conditional:

`if (ws_log_msg_is_active(WS_LOG_DOMAIN, LOG_LEVEL_DEBUG)) {
`

Hi @sstrublic, Coverity returned turned up the following:

```
*** CID 1644406:  Null pointer dereferences  (FORWARD_NULL)
/builds/wireshark/wireshark/epan/dissectors/packet-macsec.c: 433 in dissect_macsec()
427             table_index = 0;
428     
